# Line endings, settled here rather than left to whoever cloned this.
#
# The GitHub Actions Windows runner image sets core.autocrlf=true globally, so
# without this every text file arrives in the working tree with CRLF endings.
# That is not a cosmetic difference for this repository: ctest runs two design
# checks through `bash`, and a shell script whose shebang line ends in \r is
# not a script with a carriage return in it, it is a script whose interpreter
# is named "/usr/bin/env bash\r" and does not exist. The same endings also
# break every `grep -E '...$'` in those scripts, which is most of what they
# are.
#
# LF everywhere, then -- in the repository and in the working tree, on both
# platforms. Nothing here wants CRLF: MSVC compiles LF sources, and the two
# PowerShell scripts under tools/ci are as happy with one as the other.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Named rather than left to git's own detection, which is a heuristic over the
# first 8000 bytes and is only mostly right.
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.h5   binary
*.bin  binary
*.zst  binary

# Vendored verbatim, and left exactly as it was received. This is the SIL Open
# Font License as it ships with IBM Plex, CRLF endings and all; it is compiled
# into the binary as a resource and printed back by `--notices`. Normalising
# it would rewrite the bytes of a licence text this project did not write, to
# no benefit -- nothing reads it as a script.
src/gui/fonts/LICENSE.txt -text
